00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.203
In this course, you learned about the foundational concepts

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:06.973
of multi-vector retrieval, starting with text retrieval with ColBERT.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:10.076
Next, you saw how those same concepts can be used

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.879
to power multi-vector image retrieval with ColPali.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:16.549
Since multi-vector techniques generate a lot of vector data,

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:20.954
You then explored some optimization techniques to reduce ColPali's memory footprint.

00:00:21.054 --> 00:00:23.256
Then you saw how MUVERA allows

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.825
ColPali to be used with HNSW search.

00:00:25.925 --> 00:00:28.728
Finally, you explored what a working RAG

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:31.931
application built around all these techniques looks like.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.467
I hope you are leaving this course

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.237
feeling confident with the concepts underlying multi-vector retrieval.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:40.940
and with new ideas of applications you want to build.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:43.910
I can't wait to see what you come up with.
